   "source": [
    "## 2b. Team size → disruption percentile & impact — team size from OpenAlex\n",
    "\n",
    "Section 2 with the x axis moved onto our own data. `paper_metadata.author_list` is 100% null,\n",
    "so §2 borrows SciSciNet's `team_size`; here team size is the count of **distinct `author_id`s\n",
    "per work**, taken straight from the snapshot's `works_au_affs_fixed.csv.gz` in one streaming\n",
    "pass (`output/paper_team_size.parquet`, 251,654,553 works, mean 2.93).\n",
    "\n",
    "Row count is *not* team size in that file — an author with two affiliations contributes two\n",
    "rows, and only ~80% of works have `rows == distinct authors`. The rows of a work are\n",
    "contiguous in the file, so the distinct count needs no sort and no global hash.\n"
   ]
  },
